      "content": "Thanks for that. Looking at it from a policy perspective though, it seems like the \"pros\" of religious institutions—like social cohesion and moral frameworks—provide a much more tangible benefit to actual community stability than the \"cons\" of institutional friction. Given the current trend toward secularization, would you say that the loss of these religious structures is a net negative for the stability of modern societies?",
